// Written to be measured rather than to be read.
//
// It prints nothing. What it has to show is on the status line beside
// **Run**: the instructions the VM retired and the fuel they cost. Two
// million turns of this loop are about 22 million instructions, and they fit
// inside this page's 200,000,000 fuel and five seconds, so the numbers are a
// real workload's and not a scaled-down one's.
//
// The IR pane is the other half. The loop is a handful of instructions; the
// count above is what running that handful two million times comes to.
//
// This is the program `benches/arith` measures, which is where the project
// reads what a turn of a loop costs. Both are run by `web/check.mjs`, which
// fails if they ever stop being the same program.
//
// **Run & record** works on it, but the timeline keeps only its first
// moments — a few hundred turns of two million. A truncated recording of
// this one is the bound doing its job.
export fn main() -> Result<Unit, Error> {
  var total = 0
  var i = 0
  while i < 2000000 {
    if i % 7 == 0 {
      total += 1
    }
    i += 1
  }
  assertEqual(total, 285715)?
  Ok(())
}
